          "body_license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
        }
      ],
      "finding": "The new ASCO abstract and cancer-specific systematic review support a cautious systemic-opioid offer after inadequate nonpharmacologic relief in advanced cancer. The old draft is COPD-specific and must actually be replaced or changed to the instructed cancer population; the new pair does not validate the old short-acting-versus-sustained-release COPD comparison. Feedback preserves uncertainty and avoids unsupported dose/route claims.",
      "clinical_clearance": false
    },
